From: mtk23510 <mtk23510@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: FT MIC: fix MLO Reassoc Resp MIC for FT-802.1X roam

AP injected per-link RSNXE bytes (from auth->wpa_ie template) into the
Reassoc Resp FTE MIC even though the air capture shows no RSNXE in the
Resp (rsnxe_used=0, FT-802.1X) -> STA FTE-MIC validation fails -> STA
emits PMF Deauth. Gate per-link RSNXE on caller rsnxe!=NULL and align
need_ml_rsn on RX/TX so both branches pick the same MIC recipe whenever
a Basic ML element is present.

Non-MLO FT path unaffected (mlie==NULL -> need_ml_rsn stays 0).

Signed-off-by: mtk23510 <mtk23510@mediatek.com>
---
 src/common/wpa_common.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/src/common/wpa_common.c
+++ b/src/common/wpa_common.c
@@ -1023,9 +1023,11 @@
 #endif
 				}
 
-				/* fourth message, no need to add legacy rsn */
-				if (ml_info.bss_para_change_cnt_present)
-					need_ml_rsn = 1;
+				/* MLE present in this Reassoc Req -> use per-link
+				 * RSNE path on RX. Must match TX so STA's MIC
+				 * validates.
+				 */
+				need_ml_rsn = 1;
 
 				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "FT: MLO valid links=%x, need_ml_rsn=%u",
 					valid_links, need_ml_rsn);
@@ -1063,8 +1065,11 @@
 					}
 				}
 
-				if (ml_group->ml_link_num > 1)
-					need_ml_rsn = 1;
+				/* MLE will be present in this Reassoc Resp -> use
+				 * per-link RSNE path on TX. Must match RX so the
+				 * STA's MIC validates.
+				 */
+				need_ml_rsn = 1;
 
 				if (need_ml_rsn) {
 					for (i = 0; i < MAX_NUM_MLO_LINKS; i++) {
@@ -1186,7 +1191,7 @@
 	}
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_MTK_IEEE80211BE
-	if (need_ml_rsn) {
+	if (need_ml_rsn && rsnxe) {
 		for (i = 0; i < MAX_NUM_MLO_LINKS; i++) {
 			if (valid_links & BIT(i)) {
 				addr[num_elem] = link_rsnxe[i];
